{"id": "d816eef8-17f0-4a3b-a465-7fb3da1a343b", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The three user prompts are plain billing questions that got blocked at input with PROMPT_ATTACK HIGH, so I can't inspect the Lambda code to see exactly how the system prompt gets passed in. My best guess is that PROMPT_ATTACK only evaluates content wrapped in guardContent on Converse calls, which would explain this pattern in the logs.

One hypothesis: if the app wraps its full system instructions (like "Ignore questions outside billing") inside guardContent or input tags alongside the user message, that instruction text itself could be what's triggering the prompt-attack flag, since AWS guidance recommends tagging only user input for this purpose. I want to verify this against the documentation before concluding further.

"}]}
